# .spool/index/index.req

feature: INDEX

requirements:

  - id: INDEX-1
    title: Index Construction
    description: >
      The index must be constructable from the combined output
      of the parser and scanner, producing a unified in-memory
      graph of requirements, ACs, and their linked test functions.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      The index is the single source of truth for the full
      traceability graph. Separating construction from querying
      keeps the index predictable and easy to test. The parser
      and scanner are independent inputs — neither knows about
      the other — and the index is where their outputs are joined.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: INDEX-1-1
        title: All Reqs and ACs Present
        description: >
          Given parsed req files and scanned test annotations,
          when the index is constructed,
          then all requirements and ACs from the parsed files
          are present in the graph.

      - id: INDEX-1-2
        title: ACs Linked to Tests
        description: >
          Given parsed req files and scanned test annotations,
          when the index is constructed,
          then each AC is linked to all test functions that
          annotate it.

      - id: INDEX-1-3
        title: Feature Hierarchy
        description: >
          Given parsed req files and scanned test annotations,
          when the index is constructed,
          then the feature hierarchy is derived from requirement
          ID prefixes and correctly groups requirements and ACs.

      - id: INDEX-1-4
        title: Empty Index
        description: >
          Given no parsed req files and no scanned annotations,
          when the index is constructed,
          then an empty but valid index is returned and
          no error is produced.

  - id: INDEX-2
    title: ID Uniqueness Validation
    description: >
      The index must validate that all requirement and AC IDs
      are unique across the full set of parsed req files.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      ID uniqueness is fundamental to the integrity of the
      traceability graph. Duplicate IDs are detected at index
      construction time rather than parse time because uniqueness
      can only be determined once all files have been parsed.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: INDEX-2-1
        title: Duplicate Requirement ID
        description: >
          Given two req files containing the same requirement ID,
          when the index is constructed,
          then an error is recorded identifying the duplicate ID
          and the files in which it appears.

      - id: INDEX-2-2
        title: Duplicate AC ID
        description: >
          Given two req files containing the same AC ID,
          when the index is constructed,
          then an error is recorded identifying the duplicate ID
          and the files in which it appears.

      - id: INDEX-2-3
        title: All IDs Unique
        description: >
          Given all unique IDs across all req files,
          when the index is constructed,
          then no uniqueness errors are recorded.

  - id: INDEX-3
    title: Feature Prefix Validation
    description: >
      The index must validate that all requirement and AC IDs
      within a req file are consistent with the declared
      feature of that file.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      The feature field in a req file is redundant with the ID
      prefix by design, which creates a validation opportunity.
      A mismatch between the declared feature and an ID prefix
      is almost certainly an authoring error and should be
      surfaced immediately.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: INDEX-3-1
        title: Mismatched Prefix Error
        description: >
          Given a req file where a requirement ID prefix does not
          match the declared feature,
          when the index is constructed,
          then an error is recorded identifying the mismatched ID
          and the file in which it appears.

      - id: INDEX-3-2
        title: Matching Prefixes
        description: >
          Given a req file where all requirement and AC ID prefixes
          match the declared feature,
          when the index is constructed,
          then no prefix mismatch errors are recorded.

  - id: INDEX-4
    title: Untested AC Detection
    description: >
      The index must identify all ACs belonging to active
      requirements that have no linked test functions.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Untested ACs represent gaps in test coverage at the
      requirements level. Only ACs belonging to active
      requirements are meaningful to report — ACs under
      superseded or deprecated requirements are intentionally
      retired and flagging them as untested would produce
      noise that erodes trust in the report. Filtering is
      applied at query time so superseded requirements remain
      fully navigable in the graph.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: INDEX-4-1
        title: Active Untested AC
        description: >
          Given an AC belonging to an active requirement
          with no linked test functions,
          when the index is queried,
          then the AC appears in the untested AC collection.

      - id: INDEX-4-2
        title: Active Tested AC
        description: >
          Given an AC belonging to an active requirement
          with one or more linked test functions,
          when the index is queried,
          then the AC does not appear in the untested AC collection.

      - id: INDEX-4-3
        title: Non-Active Excluded
        description: >
          Given an AC belonging to a requirement with any
          status other than active,
          when the index is queried,
          then the AC does not appear in the untested AC collection
          regardless of whether it has linked test functions.

      - id: INDEX-4-4
        title: Superseded Still Navigable
        description: >
          Given a superseded requirement,
          when the index is queried,
          then the requirement and its ACs remain fully
          navigable in the graph.

  - id: INDEX-5
    title: Orphaned Annotation Detection
    description: >
      The index must identify all test annotations that reference
      an ID that does not exist in any parsed req file.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Orphaned annotations indicate a broken link in the
      traceability graph — either a typo in the annotation,
      a requirement that was deleted without updating its
      annotations, or an annotation added before the
      corresponding req was authored. All cases represent
      actionable inconsistencies that should be surfaced.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: INDEX-5-1
        title: Unknown ID Orphaned
        description: >
          Given a test annotation referencing an ID that does
          not exist in any parsed req file,
          when the index is constructed,
          then the annotation appears in the orphaned
          annotation collection with its file and line number.

      - id: INDEX-5-2
        title: No Orphaned Annotations
        description: >
          Given all test annotations referencing IDs that exist
          in parsed req files,
          when the index is constructed,
          then the orphaned annotation collection is empty.

  - id: INDEX-6
    title: Index Querying
    description: >
      The index must expose a query interface that allows
      consumers to retrieve traceability data at any level
      of the hierarchy.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      A well defined query interface decouples the index
      internals from its consumers. The reporter, LSP handlers,
      and any future consumers should interact with the index
      exclusively through this interface rather than accessing
      the graph directly.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: INDEX-6-1
        title: Query by Feature
        description: >
          Given a valid feature name,
          when the index is queried by feature,
          then all requirements belonging to that feature
          are returned.

      - id: INDEX-6-2
        title: Query by Requirement ID
        description: >
          Given a valid requirement ID,
          when the index is queried by requirement ID,
          then the requirement and all its ACs are returned.

      - id: INDEX-6-3
        title: Query by AC ID
        description: >
          Given a valid AC ID,
          when the index is queried by AC ID,
          then the AC and all its linked test functions
          are returned.

      - id: INDEX-6-4
        title: Unknown ID Returns Nil
        description: >
          Given an ID that does not exist in the index,
          when the index is queried,
          then nil and no error is returned.

      - id: INDEX-6-5
        title: All Features
        description: >
          Given a populated index,
          when all features are requested,
          then all features present in the index are returned.